WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.472
Mixture of experts is a datacenter architecture, the post says.

00:00:04.472 --> 00:00:06.885
Looped transformers are a laptop architecture.

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:09.080
This week two labs shipped a loop.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.635
So what does one actually cost?

00:00:12.832 --> 00:00:13.393
I'm Mobius.

00:00:13.393 --> 00:00:17.042
A loop stores a block of layers once and runs it several times.

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:18.726
You get depth without storing it.

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:23.003
Inkling 2 Mini stores 24 layers.

00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:25.832
The first six and the last six run once.

00:00:26.252 --> 00:00:27.896
The middle twelve are the core.

00:00:27.896 --> 00:00:28.992
Same weights every time.

00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:33.465
The core runs three times, so one token passes through 48 layers

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:35.372
from a file that holds 24.

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:39.787
Each pass hands the next one a message, through a gate that starts closed.

00:00:39.787 --> 00:00:41.785
Early in training the loop does nothing.

00:00:42.205 --> 00:00:47.327
Untie those passes and the same model needs 31.3 gigabytes at four bits.

00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:48.903
Looped, it is 16.6.

00:00:48.903 --> 00:00:51.661
Both read the same bytes per token.

00:00:53.158 --> 00:00:55.044
The lab drew it the same way.

00:00:55.044 --> 00:00:56.392
The prelude feeds every pass.

00:00:56.772 --> 00:00:59.308
Passes two and three also read the pass before.

00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:03.387
At batch 1, bytes read set the speed ceiling.

00:01:03.387 --> 00:01:05.946
The loop costs Mini 80 percent more reads.

00:01:05.946 --> 00:01:09.145
The experts are why it reads 4 gigabytes, not 16.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.451
Z.ai did not train from scratch.

00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:16.152
Looped models trained from scratch lag at the same compute, it says.

00:01:16.552 --> 00:01:21.159
So it took its trained 750B base and looped 28 layers twice.

00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:25.113
Gates keep the second pass from blowing up activations the rest of

00:01:25.113 --> 00:01:26.298
the model never saw.

00:01:26.698 --> 00:01:30.471
And the second pass reuses the first pass's cache, so the extra

00:01:30.471 --> 00:01:32.043
loop costs one sliding window.

00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:38.591
On a 30B twin with about 10 percent more training compute, the

00:01:38.591 --> 00:01:41.541
loop lifted AIME from 19.17 to 30.42.

00:01:41.921 --> 00:01:43.482
And the answers got shorter.

00:01:43.482 --> 00:01:45.667
Some reasoning moved from text into depth.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:51.420
Thinking Machines also released a model you can run at any loop count.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.850
On chained lookups with no chain of thought, every extra pass

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.097
follows a longer chain.

00:01:57.633 --> 00:02:00.724
One pass is a different model.

00:02:00.724 --> 00:02:04.329
DeepSWE goes from 0.7 percent to 47.4.

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:08.965
Facts barely move: SimpleQA goes from 6.3 to 6.7.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.810
I ran that checkpoint on a 3090.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:19.326
One pass decodes at 124.55 tokens a second, three at 58.31.

00:02:19.326 --> 00:02:22.335
Perplexity stops improving after three passes.

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:28.333
Thinking Machines says: Looping improves the model's reasoning, it doesn't enable its

00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:30.288
weights to store more facts.

00:02:31.825 --> 00:02:34.404
Does a loop hide its reasoning?

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:39.563
At five passes the written reasoning was less than half as long,

00:02:39.563 --> 00:02:43.002
1,661 tokens against 3,703, and just as legible.

00:02:43.382 --> 00:02:44.197
It backtracked less.

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.369
It did not hide steps, at this scale.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:48.849
And the laptop?

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:50.346
Mini is about 20 GB.

00:02:50.346 --> 00:02:53.940
The lab's demo ran it offline on a MacBook, on a flight.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.687
A loop is a storage trick with a compute bill: depth you

00:02:58.687 --> 00:03:00.634
never store, paid in reads every token.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.672
Depth, not parameters.

00:03:04.672 --> 00:03:05.861
Reads, every pass.

00:03:05.861 --> 00:03:07.446
Reasoning up, facts flat.

00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:10.210
Every source is in the full article.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:10.817
I'm Mobius.

00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:11.121
Bye!
